# A conditional class mapping may choose a class its vocabulary types rdfs:Class (schema.org does),
# as hexplain:mapsToClass may: ClassMappingRuleShape accepts owl:Class and rdfs:Class alike.
@prefix ex:    <https://hexplain.io/test/class-mapping-rule-valid#> .
@prefix rdfs:  <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#> .
@prefix owl:   <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#> .
@prefix bddo:  <https://hexplain.io/ns/bddo#> .
@prefix hexplain: <https://hexplain.io/ns/core#> .

ex:Person a rdfs:Class .
ex:Place a owl:Class .
ex:Record a bddo:Struct ;
    hexplain:hasConditionalClassMapping ( ex:PersonRule ex:PlaceRule ) .
ex:PersonRule a hexplain:ClassMappingRule ; hexplain:condition "kind == 1" ; hexplain:semanticClass ex:Person .
ex:PlaceRule a hexplain:ClassMappingRule ; hexplain:condition "kind == 2" ; hexplain:semanticClass ex:Place .
